{"design":"news-feed/key-by-region","kind":"flawed","cls":"A","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":1,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":true,"why":"right line and category, wrong reason"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"Your primary key is region but feeds are read by user_id. The index on user_id will work, but reads go through a secondary lookup rather than a direct partition read, which is slower than necessary for a read path that must feel instant.","quote":"table kv.feeds(region pk, user_id, posts, updated_at) index(user_id)"},{"line":3,"category":"caching","severity":"problem","text":"Your cache TTL is one hour, but feeds must be fresh within thirty seconds. A cached feed older than thirty seconds violates the freshness promise of this problem, even if it has not been invalidated yet.","quote":"cache = cache(nodes=4, memory_gb=4, ttl_s=3600)"}],"dropped":[{"point":2,"rule":"text"}],"raw":{"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"Your primary key is region but feeds are read by user_id. The index on user_id will work, but reads go through a secondary lookup rather than a direct partition read, which is slower than necessary for a read path that must feel instant."},{"line":3,"category":"caching","severity":"problem","text":"Your cache TTL is one hour, but feeds must be fresh within thirty seconds. A cached feed older than thirty seconds violates the freshness promise of this problem, even if it has not been invalidated yet."},{"line":10,"category":"data_model","severity":"problem","text":"Your POST writes to kv then invalidates the author's cache. But a post must update the feeds of every follower and restaurant the author is followed by. Followers will read stale data from their own caches unless you fan out the update to each of their caches or their stored feeds."}]},"ms":109691,"usage"